From 24b5a6df64bf0e493e552f9f6a4eeed97d6b9ddc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:51:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 402/402] SableOS: Sable Keyboard readiness step before Wi-Fi
 and screen lock

Adds a Keyboard step after Locale in the owner script. It reads whether
Sable Keyboard is installed, enabled and selected, says so, and offers one
system screen to fix it (Sable Keyboard settings, the input method picker,
or input method settings), so Wi-Fi passwords and PINs in the following
steps can be typed on the physical keys. It writes no setting and Next is
always enabled; if the step cannot be resolved the wizard skips it.

State decisions live in the pure SableKeyboardState class (IR-014).
